    "_meta":  {
                  "measured_at":  "2026-11-16",
                  "machine":  "Windows 11 Pro 10.0.26200, 16 logical cores, 1920x1080 @ 96 DPI",
                  "script":  "bench/measure_app.ps1 -Exe \u003cexe\u003e -Name \u003cname\u003e -Runs 5 (helpers in bench/BenchNative.ps1; screenshots via bench/screenshot_app.ps1)",
                  "method":  "window=first visible top-level \u003e= 300x200; idle=start of first \u003e=1000ms span with every 250ms sample \u003c 2% of 16 logical cores (tree); RAM=sum private working set 10s after idle. All numbers are the median of 5 runs, none discarded; per-run values under \u0027runs\u0027.",
                  "caveats":  [
                                  "\u0027Cold start\u0027 here means a fresh process start with a warm OS file cache (the app had been launched before); the standby list was not flushed, so true first-boot disk-cold starts would be slower for every app.",
                                  "cold_start_window_ms counts the first visible top-level window \u003e= 300x200 of the process tree. For Postman and Insomnia this window appears while the app is still showing its own in-window loading state, so cold_start_idle_ms is the better proxy for \u0027usable\u0027.",
                                  "Idle detection takes the first 1 s span in which every 250 ms sample is \u003c 2% of total machine CPU (16 cores). A quiet gap during loading (for example while waiting on network) can end it early. Postman run 2 (2665 ms against 5.6-8.5 s for the others) is likely such a case.",
                                  "idle_ram_mb = sum of private working set (Task Manager \u0027Memory\u0027 column), MB = 2^20 bytes, measured 10 s after idle. Private commit and full working set are in \u0027runs\u0027.",
                                  "Each app was measured after its first-run onboarding had been completed for the screenshots, so runs show the normal steady-state launch (Postman in Lightweight API Client mode with one history entry; Insomnia in local Scratch Pad; BloomRPC with one small proto loaded; Bruno with its auto-created sample collection and one unsaved tab).",
                                  "Screenshots: the outer window is set to 1600x1000 with SetWindowPos and the visible frame (DWMWA_EXTENDED_FRAME_BOUNDS) is captured with CopyFromScreen. Apps with a native Windows frame (Insomnia, BloomRPC) capture at 1586x993 because the invisible resize border is excluded. Postman\u0027s onboarding and login windows are fixed at 1280x800 and could not be resized."
                              ]
